# ── Python ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
**/__pycache__/**
.pytest_cache/
*.py[cod]
.venv/

# ── Julia ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Manifest.toml IS committed (root + experiments/) — it is the reproducibility record.
*.jl.cov
*.jl.*.cov
*.jl.mem
/docs/build/

# ── Reference PDFs (large; not redistributable) ───────────────────────────────
*.pdf

# ── Generated figure outputs (regenerate via the plotting scripts) ────────────
figures/
*.png
*.svg

# ── Docs / session logs ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Working notes stay LOCAL. Do not commit docs unless explicitly asked.
docs/

# ── OS noise ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store

# ── Artifacts ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# artifacts/tables.json IS committed: it is the MEASURED input (~3 KB), the provenance
# record for the model, and reviewing a diff in it is how a re-measurement gets noticed.
#
# Solved policies are NOT committed. They are build products, fully reproducible from
# tables.json + the config via `julia --project=experiments experiments/example.jl`, and
# they are large: the exported T is |S|x|A|x|S| floats, so a file is ~21 MB pretty-printed.
# Git keeps every version forever and a re-solve changes almost every line, so committing
# them would add ~21 MB of unreclaimable history per solve. The second pattern covers the
# theta-keyed names `theta_path` writes during a sweep (policy_plume_gradient=4.0.json).
artifacts/policy.json
artifacts/policy_*

# Claude Code project instructions (local only)
CLAUDE.md
claude.md

# Local verification/comparison harnesses (not committed)
scratch/
